  "description": "Hive Farm CPLA",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The application has been made under Section 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for a Certificate of Lawfulness for proposed ground levelling works. In order to grant such a certificate, the Local Planning Authority must be satisfied, on the balance of probability, that the proposed operations would be lawful if carried out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The evidence submitted in support of the application indicates that ground levelling and associated engineering operations have already commenced on site. As a result, there is ambiguity and inconsistency as to the nature and extent of the works to which the application relates, and the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the application accurately describes genuinely proposed operations capable of assessment under Section 192.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Notwithstanding this, the information provided indicates that the works comprise engineering operations which constitute development under Section 55 of the Act. On the balance of probability, the extent of the land affected exceeds 1,000 square metres and the works therefore do not fall within the limitations of Class A(e) of Part 6 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;In the absence of sufficient, clear and consistent evidence to demonstrate that the proposed works would be permitted development or otherwise lawful, the Local Planning Authority cannot conclude that the requirements of Section 192 have been met. The certificate is therefore refused.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
